# Recovered SOURCE is tracked (source-app/{lua,data-tables-lua,src,csharp,
# unity-assets}). Everything below is either an input the pipeline consumes, an
# intermediate it passes through, or a container too large for GitHub.
#
# The working tree is ~4.2 GB; the APK and two copies of BundleFragment0.bytes
# exceed GitHub's 100 MB per-file hard limit and cannot be pushed at all. The
# rules here exclude only regenerable bytes - every path below is reproduced
# deterministically by the committed pipeline from input/app.apk, so see the
# "Reproducing" section of README.md.
#
# Verify that claim rather than trusting it: the pipeline is idempotent and its
# step guards fail loudly, so a rerun either reproduces the same file counts or
# exits non-zero.

# --- inputs ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The APK under analysis, plus any other input; and the raw extraction of DEX,
# native .so, decoded resources and the Unity asset payload.
#
# Both rules are ANCHORED to the repository root on purpose. A bare `input/`
# also matches any directory named "input" at any depth, which silently
# excluded 269 recovered files under
# source-app/src/sources/androidx/compose/**/input/ (the AndroidX Compose UI
# input-handling package) - check 22 in tools/ci-checks.sh guards against a
# tracked file ever matching an ignore rule again.
/input/

/decompiled/

# --- intermediates of a decompile run (not source) --------------------------
# Original bytecode the decompiler consumes. The recovered .lua sitting next to
# it is the deliverable; keeping both would double the Lua tree for nothing.
source-app/**/*.luac

# Raw config-table bytecode extracted from assets/table/*.data. The decompiled
# .lua lives in source-app/data-tables-lua/.
source-app/data-tables/

# Extracted art binaries. 142 MB of PNG so far, and the bundle sweep is only
# 19% complete, so committing it would freeze an unfinished snapshot in
# immutable history and add ~140 MB to every resume. Reproduce with
# STEPS=bundles bash tools/decompile.sh.
source-app/game-assets/

# --- build output ---------------------------------------------------------
# build output of the Lua decompiler driver (rebuilt by tools/decompile.sh)
tools/unluac-batch/classes/

# .NET build output for the PE probe helper (rebuilt by `dotnet run`)
tools/peprobe/bin/
tools/peprobe/obj/

# --- per-run diagnostics; regenerated on each decompile run ----------------
unluac-failures.tsv
unluac-failures-tables.tsv

# Python bytecode from the CI syntax check
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS noise
.DS_Store